  "claim_short": "The proposed strengthening of Lemma 3.3 is false. Take the normalized complete Pick space H^2(D), m=1, and target multiplier phi(z)=z. If the approximants could be cyclic, the lemma's norm bound and weak-star convergence would give bounded zero-free holomorphic functions converging locally uniformly to z, contradicting Hurwitz's theorem.",
